# Checks suppressed inside this test directory only, on the same terms as the
# framework's own tests/.clang-tidy: an entry here is a check whose finding is
# *test idiom* -- a property of Catch2 -- rather than a defect. One entry, with
# the reason it cannot fire on anything worth fixing.

# bugprone-chained-comparison: `CHECK(a == b)` expands to
# `catchAssertionHandler.handleExpr(Catch::Decomposer() <= a == b)`, so the
# check sees `v0 <= v1 == v2` and reports a chained comparison. Nothing in the
# test source compares three things: the `<=` it objects to is Catch2's own
# capture hook, and both fixes it suggests -- parenthesise, or split with a
# logical operator -- would defeat the expression decomposition that makes a
# failing assertion print its two operands. Catch2 says so itself; the macro
# definition carries `/* NOLINT(bugprone-chained-comparison) */` on that very
# line in 3.15.3. CI pins catch2 3.4.0 -- ubuntu-24.04's package, which
# predates that comment -- which is why the finding reaches CI here and not on
# a workstation with a current Catch2.
#
# Directory-scoped, and no wider, for the same reason tests/.clang-tidy and
# every examples/*/tests/.clang-tidy copy is: clang-tidy offers no finer
# granularity than a directory, so this sits here rather than at `src/qt/`,
# where it would also cover non-test sources. `InheritParentConfig` keeps
# every other check the repository-root .clang-tidy enables; exactly one
# entry is subtracted, and only here.
#
# This test directory predates the gate that used to keep this suppression's
# copies in step across every Catch2 test directory (see tests/.clang-tidy's
# own note -- "the gate that checked this was removed"); it never received
# its own copy, which is why an existing test file in this same directory
# (test_forms_controller_core.cpp) carries the same idiom unflagged only
# because none of its lines had been part of a diff since it landed.

Checks: '-bugprone-chained-comparison'

InheritParentConfig: true
